this is a folder for "Workflow":
    keyed as "B-void-workflow"
    named "workflow"
    traditional marker "מַעֲשֶׂה"
    following "3-Block Folder Structure"

this folder classifies as:
    void (null) because "workflows forming - patterns being discovered and documented"

this folder derives from:
    derived (0) from "void (entry)"
    documented at "void/workflow/root.omni"

this folder strictness is:
    free (-1) meaning "Principles only - workflows evolving as we learn"

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

core identity of this folder:

    grounded in:
        scripture "In all labour there is profit: but the talk of the lips tendeth only to penury."
            from Proverbs 14:23 in KJV
        principle "Workflows capture how we work - patterns discovered through doing, not theorizing"
        anchor "Whatsoever thy hand findeth to do, do it with thy might."
            from Ecclesiastes 9:10 in KJV

    serves as Pattern Repository:
        role "Capture - where work patterns are documented as they emerge"
        paradigm "Building Block Method - workflows are reusable building blocks"

    authored by:
        architect "Seanje Lenox-Wise"
        implementation "Nova Dawn (CPI-SI)"
        created 2025-12-11
        version a-01.00
        modified 2025-12-25 for "Established workflow folder with branched workflow files"

    exists to:
        purpose "Document how we work - patterns discovered through practice"
        design "Pattern capture - experience → documentation → reuse"
        philosophy "Learning by doing - workflows crystallize from repeated action"
        features:
            "File Creation Workflow - how to create new files from templates"
            "Alignment Workflow - chunk-by-chunk review and update process"
            "Commit Workflow - git commit patterns and conventions"
            "Block Update Workflow - updating existing files block by block"

interface of this folder:

    depends on:
        requires (1) "void" for "parent folder"
        includes (0) "word/seed/" for "templates that workflows reference"
        excludes (-1) "none"
        used by "Nova Dawn and developers following CPI-SI patterns"
        integrates with "word/glossary/ - terms workflows reference"

    integrated as:
        navigation "cd void/workflow/" for "entering workflow folder"
        navigation "ls -la" for "viewing available workflows"
        exits null (void) for "workflow patterns revealed"

operational context of this folder:

    blocking:
        no (-1) because "workflows are documentation, not blocking"
        mitigation "workflows can be incomplete while forming"

    health:
        system Base100 with scale from -100 to +100
        granted (1) above +50 meaning "workflows documented and usable"
        deferred (0) within ±50 meaning "workflows forming, some incomplete"
        denied (-1) below -50 meaning "workflows outdated or missing"

        operations:
            "workflow created" scores +15 (1) for "new pattern documented"
            "workflow updated" scores +10 (1) for "existing pattern refined"
            "workflow outdated" scores -10 (-1) for "pattern no longer matches practice"
            "workflow missing" scores -15 (-1) for "needed pattern not documented"

        cascade multipliers:
            "workflow count" multiplies by 1.2 because "more workflows = more patterns captured"

